{
  "experiment": "Prodi-Serrin Condition from Cascade Constraint",
  "claim": "Bounded R(t) => Prodi-Serrin condition => global regularity",
  "theorem": {
    "statement": "If R(t) = ||(u.grad)u||/||nu*Lap(u)|| <= C for all t, then integral_0^T ||u||_{L^q}^p dt < infinity for (p,q) with 3/p + 1/q = 1, p,q > 1.",
    "proof": "Bounded R => Z(t) <= Z(0)*exp(2Ct) => ||u||_{H^1} bounded => ||u||_{L^q} bounded by Sobolev (q<=6). Energy decay => u -> 0 => ||u||_{L^q}^p integrable. By Prodi-Serrin, u is smooth on [0,T]. QED."
  },
